  "query": "I've got about $250 saved and I keep flip-flopping. Half of me wants one properly good pair of noise cancelling over-ears for my loud open-plan office; the other half says get decent wireless earbuds and a rugged little speaker for camping trips this summer, since the same money could cover both. My worry is that splitting the budget means everything ends up mediocre, and I've heard the noise cancelling in small earbuds can't physically work as well as in big cups. Is that true? Walk me through the trade-off and end with what you'd actually buy with my $250.",
